        "original_id": "4d914758-6274-52d2-b24e-2c96536c54a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Stachyuraceae, Cucurbitaceae\n- Products: Stachyurus, Cucumis, Cucumis sativus, Cucumis melo, Cucumis metuliferus, Cucumis anguria\n- Concepts: genus, species, twining plants, tendrils\n\nFacts:\n- Stachyuraceae contains a single genus with eight species.\n- Cucumis is a genus of twining, tendril-bearing plants in the Cucurbitaceae family.\n- Cucumis includes Cucumis sativus, the cucumber.\n- Cucumis includes Cucumis melo, the muskmelon, including cantaloupe and honeydew.\n- Cucumis includes Cucumis metuliferus, the horned melon.\n- Cucumis includes Cucumis anguria, the West Indian gherkin.",
